## Fix SWRL builtin atoms in inference and materialization (issue #171, PR #172)
Context: Editor-generated rules with `swrlb:` builtins over datatype
properties inferred zero triples while reporting success (#171). Four
stacked defects: bare-name builtin lookup, datatype properties missing from
the SWRL uri_map, builtin atoms joined as phantom predicates in the
inference/materialization builders, and Databricks-only `TRY_CAST` reaching
the Lakebase (Postgres) backend. Review follow-up in the same PR: IRI-safe
normalisation, shared atom partition, negated atoms as NOT EXISTS, uri_map
precedence aligned with AggregateRuleEngine, dialect gap documented.
Changes:
1. src/back/core/reasoning/SWRLBuiltinRegistry.py
   `get` / `is_builtin` accept bare names, `swrlb:` / `swrl:` prefixes and
   full IRIs via `uri_local_name` plus a known-prefix strip.
2. src/back/core/reasoning/SWRLEngine.py
   `_build_uri_map` folds class `dataProperties` into the data namespace;
   object properties are written last so they win a same-name clash, as in
   `AggregateRuleEngine._build_uri_map`.
3. src/back/core/reasoning/SWRLSQLTranslator.py
   `build_inference_sql` and `build_materialization_sql` reuse
   `SWRLParser.partition_rule_atoms`; builtin atoms become WHERE filters and
   negated atoms `NOT EXISTS`, matching `build_violation_sql`. `dialect`
   selects the SQL flavour; `dialect="postgres"` rewrites `TRY_CAST` /
   `DOUBLE`. The remaining Postgres gap (`matches`, `dateDiff`, `now`;
   CAST raising on non-numeric literals) is documented at the rewrite site.
4. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/LakebaseBase.py
   `get_query_translator` returns a Postgres-dialect translator.
5. tests/units/ontology/test_swrl_builtin_defects.py
   One regression class per defect (13 tests), including full-IRI lookup,
   object-property precedence, and negated-atom NOT EXISTS on both builders.
